I think the honest answer is you've got to do both. You can't over index on either.

1254
01:04:05,330 --> 01:04:07,761
所以这里的教训是去做实验
So the lesson here is run experiments,

1255
01:04:07,761 --> 01:04:13,610
但一定要从全局去思考结果的含义
but then make sure you think about the implication of the of the result at the bigger picture.

1256
01:04:13,810 --> 01:04:15,933
然后我们到底想做什么？要有一个计划
And then what are we trying to do? Have a plan.

1257
01:04:15,933 --> 01:04:17,770
比如我认为这个系统是这样运作的
Like I think the system works this way.

1258
01:04:17,930 --> 01:04:21,755
我有个信念：如果我们出于某某原因改变发现算法的运作方式
I have this belief that if we change the way the discovery algorithms work for XYZ

1259
01:04:21,755 --> 01:04:23,410
它会产生这样的影响
reasons, it will have this impact.

1260
01:04:24,160 --> 01:04:28,160
我能做的最小尝试是什么，来证明这一点，好，它效果很好
What's the smallest thing I can do to to prove that okay, it worked great.

1261
01:04:28,280 --> 01:04:29,840
计划 v2 不用改
No change to plan v2.

1262
01:04:30,430 --> 01:04:31,510
糟糕，那个没成
Oh, shit, that didn't work.

1263
01:04:32,710 --> 01:04:33,955
v3 就得不一样了
V3 is going to have to be different.

1264
01:04:33,955 --> 01:04:36,230
你就是想一直重复这个动作
And you just kind of want to always be going through that motion.

1265
01:04:36,710 --> 01:04:40,910
没在 YouTube 上看的观众，Tom 正在挥舞双手，比划得很夸张
People not watching in YouTube, uh, Tom is moving his hands, gesticulating wildly.

1266
01:04:42,270 --> 01:04:45,688
有没有那种场景，你会对某人说，嘿
What's like, uh, what's, what's like a context where you had said to someone, hey,

1267
01:04:45,688 --> 01:04:48,452
去拉手风琴，或者我们来拉手风琴，就是那种
go play the accordion or we're playing the accordion, like, like,

1268
01:04:48,452 --> 01:04:49,910
他们通常是哪里做错了
what are they usually doing wrong?

1269
01:04:50,390 --> 01:04:54,896
往往是你在很局部的层面上发布了东西，却没有
It tends to be that you're shipping something with it in a very local sense without

1270
01:04:54,896 --> 01:04:56,950
真正理解它的影响
necessarily understanding impact.

1271
01:04:57,070 --> 01:05:02,830
举个眼下的例子，大多数 marketplace 的核心是 listing，对吧
So an example right now is, you know, the core of most marketplaces is listings, right?

1272
01:05:02,830 --> 01:05:05,563
比如你想想 Amazon.com，如果没有 listing
Like if you try and think about Amazon dot com, without listings,

1273
01:05:05,563 --> 01:05:07,030
那基本上就什么都没有了
there's basically nothing there.

1274
01:05:07,030 --> 01:05:09,550
就剩一堆左边栏、右边栏和几个视频
It's a bunch of, you know, it's a left rail or right rail and some videos.

1275
01:05:10,410 --> 01:05:13,011
而在 video commerce 和 live commerce，或者说 Whatnot 上
Um, in video commerce and live commerce or whatnot,

1276
01:05:13,011 --> 01:05:15,370
历史上你其实并不需要 listing
you don't really historically need listings.

1277
01:05:15,530 --> 01:05:17,169
如果我想卖你一副 AirPods
If I want to sell you a pair of AirPods,

1278
01:05:17,169 --> 01:05:20,817
我完全可以把它举到屏幕前，给你看、给你描述，然后说
I could literally hold them up to screen and show you them and describe them and say,

1279
01:05:20,817 --> 01:05:21,610
这是 AirPods
they're AirPods.

1280
01:05:22,170 --> 01:05:23,330
我从 1 美元起拍
I'm going to start them at $1.

1281
01:05:23,650 --> 01:05:28,382
而作为买家，你现在已经掌握了所有需要的信息，去
And as a buyer, you now have all the information you need in order to kind of like

1282
01:05:28,382 --> 01:05:30,930
做出购买决定，这很棒
make a purchase decision, which is great.

1283
01:05:31,650 --> 01:05:36,243
所以你可能不必像别人那样投入精力去做 listing
And so you may not have to invest in making listings the way that someone else does,

1284
01:05:36,243 --> 01:05:40,092
但这对卖家可能并不好，因为做一个 listing 要花大约
and that's probably not good for a seller because it takes like three

1285
01:05:40,092 --> 01:05:45,090
三分半钟，而口头描述并举起一个东西几乎不花时间
and a/2 minutes to make a listing and it takes zero minutes to describe a thing and hold it.

1286
01:05:45,090 --> 01:05:47,805
但你随后拉远视角，会想，糟糕
Up but you then zoom out and say, oh, shit,

1287
01:05:47,805 --> 01:05:52,757
新买家会来到 live commerce，并期望搜索能正常工作
new buyers are going to come to Live Commerce and expect search to function

1288
01:05:52,757 --> 01:05:56,910
可如果我要等你卖完之后才知道你卖了什么
if I don't know what you're selling until after you've sold it.

1289
01:05:57,390 --> 01:06:01,119
那我就根本没办法把想买 AirPods 的人引到对的直播间
There's no possible way that I can put somebody in the right stream for AirPods

1290
01:06:01,119 --> 01:06:03,472
因为他们不知道，我们也不知道你有这东西
because they didn't, we didn't know you have them

1291
01:06:03,472 --> 01:06:05,480
所以我也没法把人导流过去
and I therefore can't direct people to it.

1292
01:06:05,560 --> 01:06:08,120
于是你就经历这么个过程，先说，我们不用去修它
And so you go through this exercise of like, we don't need to fix it.

1293
01:06:08,160 --> 01:06:09,680
它能用。然后你想，好，不错
It works. And then you're like, okay, great.

1294
01:06:10,200 --> 01:06:12,040
那这会对其他事情有什么影响
What does that have implications for other things?

1295
01:06:13,000 --> 01:06:14,352
好吧，那我们该怎么办？哦
Okay, then what would we do? Oh,

1296
01:06:14,352 --> 01:06:17,680
我们要让所有人都做 listing，然后你又把视角拉远一次
we're gonna make everyone make listings and you're like zoom back out again.

1297
01:06:17,720 --> 01:06:21,888
如果每个卖家现在每做一个 listing 都要花三分钟
If every seller is now spending three minutes for every listing that they're making,

1298
01:06:21,888 --> 01:06:26,056
那他们每小时能卖的东西数量就会大幅、大幅下降
the number of things they can sell per hour is now dramatically, dramatically lower,

1299
01:06:26,056 --> 01:06:27,700
这就意味着对卖家不利
which means it's bad for sellers.

1300
01:06:28,380 --> 01:06:29,740
好吧，糟糕，这我们又不能这么干
Okay, shit. We can't do that again.

1301
01:06:29,780 --> 01:06:32,163
所以你就得不断地伸缩切换，去想
And so you just, you have to keep stretching through the like,

1302
01:06:32,163 --> 01:06:35,900
我们正在做的东西有哪些更长期的影响，或者会带来哪些连锁反应
what are the longer term implications or what are the knock on effects of things we're building.

1303
01:06:36,260 --> 01:06:37,340
这非常有帮助
That is extremely helpful.

1304
01:06:37,820 --> 01:06:41,933
Whatnot 有意思的地方在于，存在这么一个光谱，一端是 Whatnot
What's interesting about whatnot is it's there's like this spectrum of like whatnot

1305
01:06:41,933 --> 01:06:44,539
另一端是整个 agentic commerce（智能体电商）的趋势
and then there's this whole trend of agentic commerce

1306
01:06:44,539 --> 01:06:47,088
由 agent（智能体）替你去购买东西
where agents are going to be buying the things for you

1307
01:06:47,088 --> 01:06:50,390
它们彼此协作，创造出一个全新的智能体经济
and just working with each other create a whole new agentic economy.

1308
01:06:50,870 --> 01:06:53,818
而 Whatnot 几乎是反过来的，人们实时互相交流
And this is like the opposite. Humans live talking to each other,

1309
01:06:53,818 --> 01:06:54,910
彼此之间做买卖
buying from each other.

1310
01:06:55,910 --> 01:07:00,350
你怎么看这个趋势，以及它可能会怎样影响你们
Thoughts on that, on that trend and, and how may, how that might impact you guys.

1311
01:07:00,910 --> 01:07:05,807
说实话，对某些事我举双手欢迎 agent 来当主宰，比如我根本不想
Listen, I for one welcome our agentic overlords for things like I don't want to have

1312
01:07:05,807 --> 01:07:08,220
去操心灯泡、空气滤芯
to think about light bulbs, air filters,

1313
01:07:08,220 --> 01:07:11,910
以及任何维持我日常生活所需的例行事务，对吧
any of the programmatic stuff that I need to run my life, right?

1314
01:07:12,390 --> 01:07:16,230
嗯，对于那些意图非常明确的事，我也很乐意交给它
Um, I'm also pretty great with it for, like, really high intent things.

1315
01:07:16,310 --> 01:07:18,150
比如我需要给电脑配一根特定的线
I need a particular cable for my computer.

1316
01:07:18,350 --> 01:07:22,137
或者我在找给家里用的户外灯
I'm looking for, you know, outdoor lights for my house,

1317
01:07:22,137 --> 01:07:25,430
这类搜索起来特别费劲的东西
things where there are really taxing searches.

1318
01:07:26,260 --> 01:07:29,475
我想想，比如要去参加婚礼，也就是说我需要一双黑皮鞋
I think about this, you know, gotta go to a wedding, which means I need black shoes,

1319
01:07:29,475 --> 01:07:32,265
但周四之前必须送到，因为如果周四前到不了
but live it by Thursday because if they don't get here before Thursday,

1320
01:07:32,265 --> 01:07:33,920
那对我就没用了，就是这类事情
they're no good for me kind of things like.

1321
01:07:34,440 --> 01:07:34,920
当然
Absolutely.

1322
01:07:35,440 --> 01:07:38,520
但在美国，大多数消费其实并不是高意图购物
But most of commerce in America isn't actually high intent.

1323
01:07:39,040 --> 01:07:43,000
电商发展到现在有多少年了？差不多有 30 年了
Like, how many years are we into ecom now? Like 30 years into ecom.

1324
01:07:43,320 --> 01:07:48,320
而电商从来没有超过美国零售支出的 20%，对吧
And e-commerce has never exceeded 20% of retail spend in America, right?

1325
01:07:48,360 --> 01:07:52,416
美国绝大绝大多数的零售购物，仍然是
The vast, vast, vast majority of retail shopping in the United States is still

1326
01:07:52,416 --> 01:07:54,600
人们亲自到店去买东西
people going in person and buying things.

1327
01:07:55,160 --> 01:07:58,080
在英国，大概是 75 比 25 这样的比例
In the UK, it's somewhere, it's like 75, 25.

1328
01:07:58,640 --> 01:08:02,560
事实证明，其实很多购物都是低意图的
And it turns out, actually, that a lot of shopping is low intent.

1329
01:08:03,560 --> 01:08:04,520
比如我去逛商场
I'm going to the mall.

1330
01:08:05,040 --> 01:08:08,400
可能是因为快要参加婚礼，却没有合适的衣服穿
I might be because I've got a wedding coming up and I don't have anything to wear.

1331
01:08:08,440 --> 01:08:11,284
于是我到处逛逛，看看有什么可选的
And I'm going to wander around and see what people have available

1332
01:08:11,284 --> 01:08:13,760
因为我其实并不清楚自己具体想要什么
because I don't actually know specifically what I want.

1333
01:08:14,350 --> 01:08:18,755
实体店的价值其实在于，经营
And actually, the value of stores is that that person who runs

1334
01:08:18,755 --> 01:08:24,110
那家鞋店的人有主见、有品味，她精心挑选了一批鞋子
that shoe store has agency and taste, and she curates a selection of shoes.

1335
01:08:24,870 --> 01:08:27,110
她提供一定水准的客户服务
She has, you know, a level of customer service.

1336
01:08:27,310 --> 01:08:30,989
她有橱窗展示，能让我看到她店里有哪些款式
She has a window display which can show me the types of things she has

1337
01:08:30,989 --> 01:08:32,698
我可以在商场里逛来逛去
and I can wander around the mall

1338
01:08:32,698 --> 01:08:36,180
慢慢弄清楚自己想买什么，或者从中获得启发
and actually work out what it is I want to buy or be educated by it.

1339
01:08:36,620 --> 01:08:38,660
事实证明，这个过程其实相当愉快
And as it turns out, it's quite pleasant.

1340
01:08:38,660 --> 01:08:41,300
商场之所以是一种社交场合，是有原因的
Like there's a reason that the mall is a social thing.

1341
01:08:41,700 --> 01:08:46,180
所以我认为，agentic 会是一个巨大的方向
And so I think, you know, that Agentic is going to be huge.

1342
01:08:46,980 --> 01:08:50,947
不过零售在美国是一个 7.5 万亿美元的产业
Retail is a seven and a half trillion dollar industry in the US though,

1343
01:08:50,947 --> 01:08:53,820
所以我不觉得这是赢家通吃的局面
so I don't think it's a like winner takes all thing.

1344
01:08:54,060 --> 01:08:56,965
我认为直播电商做到的，是第一次
What I think Live Commerce does is it's the first time

1345
01:08:56,965 --> 01:09:00,266
我们能够把互联网的规模
that we've ever managed to kind of like bring together scale

1346
01:09:00,266 --> 01:09:03,764
和便利结合起来，同时又保留那种
and convenience of the internet and also that same kind of like,

1347
01:09:03,764 --> 01:09:06,537
实体购物的社交文化体验
social cultural experience of physical shopping

1348
01:09:06,537 --> 01:09:09,970
因为你知道，在 Twitch 我们基本上会假设
because you know at at Twitch we used to basically assume that.

1349
01:09:09,970 --> 01:09:11,793
如果一场直播的观众少于 1000 人
If it's less than 1,000 people in a stream,

1350
01:09:11,793 --> 01:09:14,450
就不划算，因为你是靠 CPM 来运营的
it's non economic because you're you're operating on CPM's.

1351
01:09:15,130 --> 01:09:18,810
但你在 Whatnot 上进入一场直播，可能只看到三五十个人
