1352
01:09:19,010 --> 01:09:22,480
你想象一下，你在商场里经营一家鞋店
And you, you imagine for a moment that you're running a shoe store at a mall

1353
01:09:22,480 --> 01:09:24,130
而店里有 50 个人
and you had 50 people in your store.

1354
01:09:24,250 --> 01:09:25,170
你永远不会关门
You'd never close.

1355
01:09:25,810 --> 01:09:29,074
你几乎永远不会关店，因为这
Like you would literally never shut down the store because that's

1356
01:09:29,074 --> 01:09:32,337
比你能想象的实体店客流量要大得多
so much more foot traffic than you can ever imagine being in a store

1357
01:09:32,337 --> 01:09:35,779
因为电商和娱乐的经济模型完全不同
because commerce has totally different economics to entertainment

1358
01:09:35,779 --> 01:09:38,509
CPM 根本不是你需要担心的东西
and CPM's aren't the thing that you have to worry about.

1359
01:09:38,509 --> 01:09:40,170
所以我觉得它并不真的是
So I think it's not really in kind.

1360
01:09:40,170 --> 01:09:41,939
和 agentic 的直接竞争
Of like competition with Agentic,

1361
01:09:41,939 --> 01:09:45,110
我觉得它满足的是完全不同的客户需求
I think it's completely different kind of like customer need.

1362
01:09:45,870 --> 01:09:47,644
太棒了，大家都有各自的空间
Amazing. There's room for everyone.

1363
01:09:47,644 --> 01:09:49,990
也许我想用一个关于 Twitter 的问题来结束
I want to end maybe with a question about Twitter.

1364
01:09:50,110 --> 01:09:53,470
你曾经在 Twitter 工作过？是的，在 Twitter 做增长方向的 PM
So you were at Twitter? Yes, sir. A PM at Twitter working on growth.

1365
01:09:54,110 --> 01:09:56,446
我感觉每个在 Twitter 工作过的人
I feel like everybody that worked at Twitter

1366
01:09:56,446 --> 01:09:59,350
作为 PM，都被那段 Twitter 的经历留下了创伤
as a PM was just scarred from the experience of Twitter.

1367
01:09:59,390 --> 01:10:01,408
每个人都说千万别这样做事。有没有，呃
Everyone's do not do things this way. What's, uh,

1368
01:10:01,408 --> 01:10:03,870
那段经历里有什么让你记忆深刻的东西
what's something that stuck with you from that experience?

1369
01:10:03,910 --> 01:10:06,030
你学到了什么？又抛弃了哪些旧观念？说来有趣
What did you learn? What you unlearn? It is funny.

1370
01:10:06,190 --> 01:10:07,938
我，呃，我以前跟一个朋友说过
I, uh, I have said to a friend before

1371
01:10:07,938 --> 01:10:10,710
让一个在 2015、
that asking someone who was at Twitter in like the 2015,

1372
01:10:10,710 --> 01:10:15,230
16 年那段时期在 Twitter 待过的人回忆，有点像治疗师让人讲述自己的童年
16 era is a little bit like a therapist asking somebody to tell them about their childhood.

1373
01:10:15,270 --> 01:10:17,590
就是那种，你知道的，被勾起来的创伤
It's like, you know, the trauma that you're, you're bringing up.

1374
01:10:18,030 --> 01:10:18,470
是啊
Yeah.

1375
01:10:18,670 --> 01:10:20,455
对于不熟悉那段往事的人来说
For those who not familiar with that lore,

1376
01:10:20,455 --> 01:10:23,310
我在那儿的两年里，我们换了九任产品负责人
I think we had nine heads of product in the two years that I was there.

1377
01:10:23,350 --> 01:10:24,670
混乱就到了那种程度
It was that level of kind of chaos.

1378
01:10:24,870 --> 01:10:27,681
我最喜欢的一句话是合作团队的一个人说的
I think my favorite quote was from someone on the partnerships team who said,

1379
01:10:27,681 --> 01:10:29,350
他说感觉就像活在层出不穷的戏码里
it felt like Caris, wish I lived in the events.

1380
01:10:29,680 --> 01:10:32,560
那就是那地方各种狗血剧情发生的频率
That was like how often drama was going on about the place.

1381
01:10:33,200 --> 01:10:37,045
嗯，Lenny，我觉得我从
Um, I think, Lenny, I probably took two overwhelming things away from,

1382
01:10:37,045 --> 01:10:40,760
在 Twitter 的那段时间里，除了结识一些很棒的朋友之外，大概带走了两个特别深刻的收获
from my time at Twitter and other than like some incredible friends.

1383
01:10:40,800 --> 01:10:43,057
我得说，从那个时代的 Twitter
And I will say that the, the product diaspora from

1384
01:10:43,057 --> 01:10:45,920
走出来的产品人才真的很惊人，如今遍地都是
that era of Twitter is pretty incredible and, and everywhere.

1385
01:10:46,600 --> 01:10:50,004
第一个是，如果你真的找到了产品市场契合度
The first one is like if you truly find product market fit,

1386
01:10:50,004 --> 01:10:52,344
如果你真的抓住了那道闪电
like if you manage to bottle lightning,

1387
01:10:52,344 --> 01:10:56,245
那么无论你把组织搞得多糟
doesn't matter how badly you screw up the organization, uh, of it,

1388
01:10:56,245 --> 01:11:00,854
它依然是巨大的，Twitter 确实达到了那种程度的产品市场契合度
like it's huge and like Twitter genuinely had that level of product market fit

1389
01:11:00,854 --> 01:11:02,840
那是你能在情感上感受到的
that you could emotionally feel.

1390
01:11:03,280 --> 01:11:04,678
人们有多爱你的产品
How much people loved your product.

1391
01:11:04,678 --> 01:11:07,800
在职业生涯相对早期就学到这一点，是一个非常有力的试金石
And it's a really powerful litmus test to learn relatively early in your career.

1392
01:11:07,960 --> 01:11:12,340
这才是 PMF，而不是说，嘿，图表看起来还行，对吧
And that's what PMF is not like, hey, the graphs look okay, right?

1393
01:11:12,380 --> 01:11:14,100
里面有一种狂热的程度
There's like a level of fervor that goes in.

1394
01:11:14,980 --> 01:11:19,624
嗯，另一面比较不那么正面的，是我肯定
Um, I think maybe on the flip side of like less positive is like what it definitely

1395
01:11:19,624 --> 01:11:23,714
学到的一点：大多数时候你听说事情很复杂，其实并不是
Learned is like most of the time you hear it's really complex it it isn't

1396
01:11:23,714 --> 01:11:25,100
只是领导力太弱了
leaderships just weak.

1397
01:11:25,820 --> 01:11:28,788
就拿我在那儿的那两年来说
So, you know, the two years that I was there,

1398
01:11:28,788 --> 01:11:33,900
所有人都知道我们迟早得取消 140 字的限制，对吧
everyone knew we were going to have to lift the 140 character limit, right?

1399
01:11:33,900 --> 01:11:38,593
一个又一个工作组，"超越 140" 这个项目
There was working group after working group, like the project beyond 140 was, like,

1400
01:11:38,593 --> 01:11:41,609
到处都是，因为我们知道，比如说
everywhere because we knew, for example, that, like,

1401
01:11:41,609 --> 01:11:45,900
日本用户发推的频率是西方市场用户的六倍
people in Japan tweeted six times more often than people in western markets.

1402
01:11:45,980 --> 01:11:48,106
我们跟他们交流后发现，很大程度上
And it was largely when we spoke to them

1403
01:11:48,106 --> 01:11:52,758
是因为在相同字数下，汉字能表达的内容比
because kanji let you say heaps more in the same number of characters than, you know,

1404
01:11:52,758 --> 01:11:54,020
罗曼语系多得多
romance language did.

1405
01:11:54,590 --> 01:11:56,456
