1447
01:14:01,560 --> 01:14:03,894
所以具体的例子可能实在太多了
So there's probably just too many specific examples of,

1448
01:14:03,894 --> 01:14:05,434
那些我在职业生涯中搞砸的时候
of times I've screwed up in my career,

1449
01:14:05,434 --> 01:14:07,520
但它们背后可能有个很常见的共性
but there probably is a really common thread to it.

1450
01:14:07,760 --> 01:14:12,230
我觉得这可能是任何 PM 都容易掉进去的陷阱，就是说
And I think it's probably an easy trap for, for any PM to fall into, which is like,

1451
01:14:12,230 --> 01:14:16,565
呃，平均值对具体个体毫无意义，这大概是让我
um, averages mean nothing to the individual is probably the thing that I've,

1452
01:14:16,565 --> 01:14:17,920
真正吃过大亏的一点
like really scarred by.

1453
01:14:18,760 --> 01:14:21,741
呃，在任何规模够大的群体里，你会很想去
Uh, in any sizable population, it's really attractive to go

1454
01:14:21,741 --> 01:14:25,021
看某个功能的平均使用率或平均采用率
and look at like average utility or average adoption of something

1455
01:14:25,021 --> 01:14:26,869
然后你会发现，你懂的
and then you find that like, you know,

1456
01:14:26,869 --> 01:14:29,552
只有 3% 的人用某个功能，你就想，行啊
only 3% of people use something and you're like, cool,

1457
01:14:29,552 --> 01:14:31,520
我们大概可以把这个功能砍掉
we can probably get rid of that feature.

1458
01:14:31,600 --> 01:14:32,600
用的人不多
It's not used widely.

1459
01:14:33,180 --> 01:14:36,560
但如果你不再深入一层想想，其实对于，你懂的
But if you don't go a layer deeper and be like, actually for like, you know,

1460
